<Defs>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       THE GLITTERTECH RESEARCH GATE

       All 18 of Ushanka's projects inherit techLevel Ultra from
       USE_GE_ProjectBase, so More Realistic Research would auto-generate
       Theoretical 5 + Experimental 4 for every one of them. We list all 18
       anyway, for three reasons.

       1. CONTROL. Experimental points pool PER TYPE, not per material. If a
          project's pool is {Steel, Plasteel, Glittercore}, every point can be
          paid in steel. Auto-generation therefore cannot enforce a specific
          material. One material per project is the only way to make the cost
          mean anything.

       2. TWO PROJECTS ARE OTHERWISE DEAD. Auto-generation picks study
          subjects from the things a project UNLOCKS, which you cannot build
          until the research is done. Usually harmless, because UnlockedDefs
          also contains recipe products you can find or buy. But
          USH_DarkGlitterpanelsRes unlocks only USH_DarkGlitterpanel, and
          USH_MolecularDisassemblerRes only USH_GlittertechRepairer and
          USH_MolecularDisassembler. None of those three appears in any
          layout, prefab, loot table or trader stock, so both projects would
          be permanently unresearchable, silently.
          Re-check with `python tools/audit_research.py` after any mod change.

       3. COST SHAPE. Auto-generation's Theoretical 5 is 90 study sessions
          across the tree. That is dead pawn time, not a gate.

       =====================================================================
       THE THREE ANALYSIS TYPES  (verified against the decompiled DLL)

         reverseEngineering  never consumed. It takes deterioration damage,
                             but USH_Glitterheart sets useHitPoints false so
                             not even that. Own one, study it, keep it. GATE.
         experimental        consumes exactly one item per point. COST.
         theoretical         never consumed, pure delay. Not used here.

       Gate and cost sit in separate point pools, so neither can be paid off
       with the other.
       =====================================================================

       THE DESIGN

       ONE hard gate, on the root. Every one of the 18 projects traces back to
       USH_GlittertechFabrication, so gating that one project gates the whole
       tree exactly once. It costs a glitterheart you must POSSESS, not spend:
       you cannot get one without going to orbit, and you still have it after.
       Ushanka already charges hearts to BUILD glittertech, so charging them
       again to research it would be paying twice for the same trip.

       Everything downstream costs materials, not hearts:

         ComponentSpacer   shallow branches. Spacer tier deliberately, because
                           plasteel is far too easy to come by to stand in for
                           glitterworld research.
         USH_Glittercore   deep branches. Crafted at the glittertech
                           fabricator, which the root unlocks and which itself
                           costs a glitterheart to build. The deep tree runs
                           on output from the machine the gate bought you.

       Whole-tree total: 28 spacer components, 21 glittercores, and exactly
       ONE glitterheart, never consumed. Cheap enough not to be a second grind
       stacked on top of flying to orbit; expensive enough that you are stood
       at the bench for a reason.

       TO TUNE: move the pointsRequired values before changing materials. The
       material is the story, the points are the dial.

       EVERY DEF BELOW IS MayRequire="sae.researchmod". ManualAnalysisDef is
       ResearchMakesSense's own def type, supplied by More Realistic Research's
       assembly. With MRR disabled, as it is in the MVP multiplayer set, an
       ungated def of that type makes RimWorld log "could not find type" once
       per def at startup. Eighteen red errors that mean nothing. MayRequire
       drops them cleanly instead, and restores them the moment MRR is back.

       NOTE: XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen. Use "=" for rules.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <!-- ===================== The gate ===================== -->

  <ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef MayRequire="sae.researchmod">
    <defName>Archinity_GT_Fabrication</defName>
    <researchProject>USH_GlittertechFabrication</researchProject>
    <!-- The only glitterheart requirement in the tree. Possess, not spend. -->
    <reverseEngineeringMaterials>
      <li>USH_Glitterheart</li>
    </reverseEngineeringMaterials>
    <reverseEngineeringPointsRequired>2</reverseEngineeringPointsRequired>
    <experimentalMaterials>
      <li>ComponentSpacer</li>
    </experimentalMaterials>
    <experimentalPointsRequired>4</experimentalPointsRequired>
  </ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef>

